# BSKP: Skip next location if condition is true - Bit operation instructions
# Based on C# emulator analysis from Instructions.BitOperationInstructions.cs:
# - BSKP ZRO: Skip if bit = 0 (opcode "0175000" octal = 0xFD00)
# - BSKP ONE: Skip if bit = 1 (opcode "0175200" octal = 0xFD80)
# - BSKP BCM: Skip if bit ≠ K (opcode "0175400" octal = 0xFE00)
# - BSKP BAC: Skip if bit = K (opcode "0175600" octal = 0xFE80)
#
# The C# implementation shows these increment P when condition is true
# Format: bits 6-3 = bit number, bits 2-0 = register
#
# SLEIGH Limitation: 9-bit mask exceeds 8-bit limitation
# However, we can implement this as documentation with correct P-code semantics

# P-code implementation (documented - cannot compile due to 9-bit mask):
# BSKP ZRO:
# local reg_val:2 = GetRopRegister(dr);
# local bit_is_zero:1 = ((reg_val >> bn) & 1) == 0;
# if (bit_is_zero) P = P + 1;
#
# BSKP ONE:
# local reg_val:2 = GetRopRegister(dr);
# local bit_is_one:1 = ((reg_val >> bn) & 1) != 0;
# if (bit_is_one) P = P + 1;
#
# BSKP BCM:
# local reg_val:2 = GetRopRegister(dr);
# local bit_val:1 = (reg_val >> bn) & 1;
# if (bit_val != STS[K]) P = P + 1;
#
# BSKP BAC:
# local reg_val:2 = GetRopRegister(dr);
# local bit_val:1 = (reg_val >> bn) & 1;
# if (bit_val == STS[K]) P = P + 1;
#
# Manual SLEIGH would require:
# :BSKP_ZRO bn, dr is token_175000 & bn & dr {
#     local bit_val:1 = (dr >> bn) & 1;
#     if (bit_val == 0) { P = P + 1; }
# }